{
  "$comment": "#NEW-144 (part of #NEW-143): THE PROTOCOL BASE of Exponential's MCP endpoints (`/api/mcp`, `/api/mcp/apps`) for MCP 2026-07-28 next to the 2025 handshake. ERAS (`versions`): a request whose `params._meta` carries `metaKeys.protocolVersion` is MODERN (2026-07-28: stateless, no handshake, `server/discover` answers the versions and capabilities, every request carries its client's capabilities); anything else is LEGACY (2025-06-18 / 2025-11-25: `initialize` still answers, its `params.capabilities` are the client's only on that one request; every later legacy request reads as a client that declared nothing). THE CLIENT (`clientCases`): the gate reads the per-request envelope ONCE (`clientContextOf`) and every handler gets it as `ctx.client`: era, protocolVersion, clientInfo, the raw capabilities, the `extensions` map, and the derived flags (`elicitation.form` = `elicitation: {}` or `elicitation.form`; `elicitation.url` only when declared; `tasks` = extension `io.modelcontextprotocol/tasks`; `ui` = extension `io.modelcontextprotocol/ui`; `sampling`, `roots`). A capability nobody declared is false; a malformed envelope reads as nothing declared. THE SERVER'S EXTENSIONS (`serverExtensions`): one map in one place (`lib/emcp/extensions.ts`), declared in `capabilities.extensions` of both `initialize` and `server/discover` for callers outside a session; an extension enters the map only with its handlers (#NEW-147: skills and tasks). MRTR (`mrtr`): only `tools/call`, `prompts/get` and `resources/read` may answer `resultType: \"input_required\"` (`inputRequiredMethods`), with at least one of `inputRequests` / `requestState`; an input request goes out only when the client declared its capability (`deliverCases`: form elicitation needs `elicitation.form`, url needs `elicitation.url`, sampling `sampling`, roots `roots`); a declined, cancelled or missing answer reads as no answer (`answerCases`). REQUEST STATE (`stateCases`): Exponential's `requestState` is AEAD-sealed (AES-256-GCM, key = HKDF-SHA256 of BETTER_AUTH_SECRET, salt `stateKey.salt`, info `stateKey.info`; wire = `stateKey.prefix` + base64url(iv | ciphertext | tag)) over the claims {v, sub = the member, grant = the credential (`oauth:<clientId>`, `key:<keyId>` or `member`), method, tool, args = base64url SHA-256 of the canonical JSON of the call's arguments (audit.json's canonical JSON, no arguments = `{}`), exp = mint + `ttlSeconds`, jti, data = the handler's own state}; it redeems ONCE: the first check that fails names the refusal in this order: `expired` (now >= exp), `member`, `grant`, `method`, `tool`, `args`, `replayed` (the jti was already redeemed); a state that does not open (tampered, another key, malformed) is `sealed`. Every refusal answers JSON-RPC -32602 `Invalid or expired requestState` (the SDK's frozen wording), never the reason. ERRORS (`errors`): the 2026-07-28 codes. GOLDENS (`spec`): the spec's own examples, verbatim (comments stripped); `discoverResultKeys` are the keys every `server/discover` result of ours carries.",
